<title>UK: HORSE RACING-ENGLISH 2,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-ENGLISH 2,000 GUINEAS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>NEWMARKET, England 1997-05-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the English</p>
<p>2,000 Guineas, a group one race for three-year-old colts and</p>
<p>fillies, run over one mile (1.6 km) on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Entrepreneur  11-2 (ridden by Michael Kinane)</p>
<p> 2. Revoque	100-30 favourite (John Reid)</p>
<p> 3. Poteen	   9-1 (Pat Eddery)</p>
<p>16 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Three-quarters of a length, one and a half</p>
<p>lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Michael Tabor and trained at Newmarket by</p>
<p>Michael Stoute.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 131,832 pounds sterling ($210,000).</p>
</text>
